Accordingly, I pass the following:
ORDER i) The appeal is allowed-in-part;
ii) The judgment and award dated 23.09.2022 passed in MVC No.982/2019 by the Senior Civil Judge and Motor Accident Claims Tribunal, Pavagada, is modified;
iii) The claimants would be entitled to a sum of Rs.15,25,244/- as against Rs.9,68,060/-;
iv) The interest awarded by the tribunal at the rate of 8% per annum on the compensation amount of Rs.9,68,060/- is left undisturbed.

The enhanced compensation shall carry interest at the rate of 6% per annum;
v) The compensation amount shall be paid by the respondent-Insurance Company within a period of - 10 - NC: 2024:KHC:6647 four weeks from the date of receipt of a copy of this judgment;
vi) The compensation amount shall be released in favour of claimant No.1 in accordance to the share stipulated by the tribunal and remaining amount shall be released in favour of other claimants in accordance to the apportionment of shares stipulated by the tribunal;
vii) All other terms and conditions stipulated by the tribunal shall stand intact;
viii) The tribunal is justified in the aspect of pay and recovery procedure, in view of the plea taken that the rider of the motor cycle did not possess a valid and effective driving licence as on the date of occurrence of accident and the same is retained.

